  "solution": {
    "text": "OEH is an equipotential surface, the uniform electric field must be perpendicular to it pointing from higher to lower potential as shown.<br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0064_21cac740d6af.jpg\" /><br /><br />Hence <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>–</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mtext>E=</mtext><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mtext>(v</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>E</mtext></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>–v</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>B</mtext></mrow></msub><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>EB</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>0–(–2)</mtext></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mtext>2</mtext></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mtext>2</mtext></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>→</mo></mrow></mover><mover><mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mtext> </mtext><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>–</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>–</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mover></math>"
